e>DINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Specifies the current bias, in minutes, for local time translation on this computer.
						The bias is the difference, in minutes, between Coordinated Universal Time (UTC) and local time.
						UTC = local time + bias ]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>standardName</Name><Type>STRING(31)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Specifies a null-terminated string associated with standard time
								on this operating system. ]]></Comment><BitSize>256</BitSize><BitOffs>32</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>standardDate</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Utilities">TIMESTRUCT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[Specifies a SYSTEMTIME structure that contains a date and local time when the
								transition from daylight saving time to standard time occurs on this operating system.]]></Comment><BitSize>128</BitSize><BitOffs>288</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>standardBias</Name><Type>DINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Specifies a bias value to be used during local time translations that occur during standard time. ]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>416</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>daylightName</Name><Type>STRING(31)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Specifies a null-terminated string associated with daylight saving time on this operating system.
								For example, this member could contain "PDT" to indicate Pacific Daylight Time.]]></Comment><BitSize>256</BitSize><BitOffs>448</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>daylightDate</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Utilities">TIMESTRUCT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Specifies a SYSTEMTIME structure that contains a date and local time when the transition
								from standard time to daylight saving time occurs on this operating system. ]]></Comment><BitSize>128</BitSize><BitOffs>704</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>daylightBias</Name><Type>DINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Specifies a bias value to be used during local time translations that occur during daylight saving time. ]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>832</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name>E_SystemState</Name><BitSize>16</BitSize><BaseType>INT</BaseType><EnumInfo><Text>InitController</Text><Enum>0</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Controller Initialization (one-shot config, params, PID setup)]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>SesOff</Text><Enum>70</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ SES Off (idle / standby, waiting for SES ON command)]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>CheckIfHot</Text><Enum>10</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Check if system was just running (hot restart shortcut)]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>FillWater</Text><Enum>20</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ SES Initialization - Fill Water]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>PurgeVessel</Text><Enum>30</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ SES Initialization - Purge Vessel]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>SetDiffPressure</Text><Enum>40</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ SES Initialization - Setting Differential Pressure]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>InitMain</Text><Enum>50</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ SES Initialization - Main (final checks before flow)]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>SteamFlowing</Text><Enum>60</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Steam Flowing (normal production, PID flow control)]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>Maintenance</Text><Enum>80</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Maintenance mode (manual actuation, loopback)]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>Fault</Text><Enum>99</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Fault (latched; operator reset returns to InitController)]]></Comment></EnumInfo><Properties><Property><Name>qualified_only</Name></Property><Property><Name>strict</Name></Property><Property><Name>to_string</Name></Property><Property><Name>generate_implicit_init_function</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>ST_ProcessValues</Name><Comment><![CDATA[=============================================================================
 ST_ProcessValues
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Live process data in ENGINEERING UNITS (Torr, degC, SLM).
 Populated by FB_FlowCalc / analog input scaling, consumed by FB_Hmi,
 FB_FaultMonitor and FB_PressureControl.
 pack_mode 1 so pyads structure_def offsets are byte-exact.
=============================================================================]]></Comment><BitSize>496</BitSize><SubItem><Name>rPt1Upstream</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ PT-1 upstream pressure    ]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rPt2Downstream</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ PT-2 downstream pressure  ]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>32</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rDiffPressure</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ PT-1 - PT-2 differential]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rDiffPressureOffset</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ pt1-pt2 differential when equalized]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>96</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rAtmPressure</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ atmospheric pressure - computed]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>128</BitOffs><Default><Value>760</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rTc1Spa</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ TC1 SPA temperature]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>160</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rTc2FlowMeter</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ TC2 flow meter temperature]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>192</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rTc3External</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ TC3 external heater temperature]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>224</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rTc4Delivery</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ TC4 delivery line temperature]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>256</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rFlowActual</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ F3 calculated steam flow     ]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>288</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rFlowSetpoint</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ active flow setpoint         ]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>320</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rFlowRated</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ rated max flow    ]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>352</BitOffs><Default><Value>25</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rFlowRatio</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ FL_TO_DP23 = F3 / DP23 --> units: SLM per Torr  ]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>384</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rCondensateFlow</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ flow through the small (drain/condensate) orifice         ]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>416</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bWaterHigh</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ water at high limit --> high limit switch on]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>448</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bWaterFull</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ full water level --> center limit switch on, high off]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>456</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bWaterLow</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ low water level --> low limit switch on, center/high off]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>464</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bWaterEmpty</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ empty water level --> low limit switch off    ]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>472</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bPowerFaultSensor</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ power fault sensor]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>480</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bCabinetFloodSensor</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ cabinet flood sensor]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>488</BitOffs></SubItem><Properties><Property><Name>pack_mode</Name><Value>1</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>FB_ProcessCalcs</Name><BitSize>928</BitSize><SubItem><Name>eState</Name><Type>E_SystemState</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>32</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>stProcessValues</Name><Type>ST_ProcessValues</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ this FB is the only writer]]></Comment><BitSize>496</BitSize><BitOffs>48</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rCurrentMeasRange</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ 16bit signed INT --> 0-32767 is positive range]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>544</BitOffs><Default><Value>32767</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rSensorPressRange</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ 0-30psia --> 0-1551.45torr]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>576</BitOffs><Default><Value>1551.45</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rDp12</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ flow calculations]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>608</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rDp23</Name><Type>REAL</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>640</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rFlowActual</Name><Type>REAL</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>672</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rOrificeA1_25</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ main orifice coefficient]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>704</BitOffs><Default><Value>0.05946087</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rOrificeA1_50</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ main orifice coefficient]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>736</BitOffs><Default><Value>0.09</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rOrificeA2</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ condensate/drain path coefficient]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>768</BitOffs><Default><Value>0.001057082</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rOrificeA3</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ SPA path coefficient]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>800</BitOffs><Default><Value>0.01</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rOrificeB1</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ main orifice offset]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>832</BitOffs><Default><Value>0</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rOrificeB2</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ condensate offset]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>864</BitOffs><Default><Value>0</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rOrificeB3</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ torr offset]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>896</BitOffs><Default><Value>40</Value></Default></SubItem><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>E_FaultId</Name><Comment><![CDATA[=============================================================================
 E_FaultId
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Identifies WHICH fault tripped first. FB_FaultMonitor latches one of these
 on the transition from healthy to faulted and holds it until ResetAll().

 The numeric values are the legacy HMI message-table indices, so the existing
 message strings on the panel keep working without a translation layer.
 Where the legacy reused one index for several distinct causes, the causes
 are split into separate IDs here and the duplicated index is noted.
=============================================================================]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BaseType>INT</BaseType><EnumInfo><Text>None</Text><Enum>0</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>PowerFault</Text><Enum>1</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ --- hardware / utilities -------------------------------------------]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>CabinetFlood</Text><Enum>2</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>PneumaticLow</Text><Enum>3</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>UpstreamOverPress</Text><Enum>11</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ --- pressure -------------------------------------------------------]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>DownstreamOverPress</Text><Enum>12</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>DownstreamStartHigh</Text><Enum>13</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>StartupDiffPressTimeout</Text><Enum>14</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>Pt1Hardware</Text><Enum>15</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>Pt2Hardware</Text><Enum>16</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>StartupDiffPressXCheck</Text><Enum>17</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Transducer cross-check failure. Legacy shared index 58 with the
 timeout above; split so first-out can tell them apart. Point the HMI
 message table at 58 if a distinct string is not wanted.]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>WaterFill</Text><Enum>21</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ --- water ----------------------------------------------------------]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>WaterRegulation</Text><Enum>22</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>WaterEmpty</Text><Enum>23</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>WaterOverFill</Text><Enum>24</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>VesselPurgeTimeout</Text><Enum>25</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>SpaOverTemp</Text><Enum>31</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ --- temperature: over-limit ----------------------------------------]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>FlowMeterOverTemp</Text><Enum>32</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>ExternalOverTemp</Text><Enum>33</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>DownstreamOverTemp</Text><Enum>34</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>SpaWarmupTimeout</Text><Enum>41</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ --- temperature: warm-up failures ----------------------------------]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>FlowMeterWarmupTimeout</Text><Enum>42</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>ExternalWarmupTimeout</Text><Enum>43</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>DownstreamWarmupTimeout</Text><Enum>44</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>ExternalNoTempRise</Text><Enum>51</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Legacy reused index 76 for all three external-line faults. Split so
 the operator can tell "TC not bonded to heater" from "line went cold".]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>ExternalLowAtReady</Text><Enum>52</Enum></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>FlowRateError</Text><Enum>61</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ --- flow -----------------------------------------------------------]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>HmiCommLoss</Text><Enum>300</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ --- new in this system ---------------------------------------------]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>TimeSetFault</Text><Enum>301</Enum></EnumInfo><Properties><Property><Name>qualified_only</Name></Property><Property><Name>strict</Name></Property><Property><Name>to_string</Name></Property><Property><Name>generate_implicit_init_function</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>ST_Faults</Name><Comment><![CDATA[=============================================================================
 ST_Faults
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 One named BOOL per fault, replacing the legacy B1600.x / B1601.x / B1602.x
 bit-of-word addressing. Names taken from the element documentation table
 in the DS6 source. Legacy address noted per field for commissioning.
 pack_mode 1: each BOOL = 1 byte, so pyads can map this with a simple
 structure_def or read it as a byte array.
