ard">TON</Type><BitSize>224</BitSize><BitOffs>7488</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rExtTempAtStart</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ external temperature captured at cold start]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>7712</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bExtRiseArmed</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>7744</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bExtRiseTested</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>7752</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>tonFlowRatio</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">TON</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ --- flow ratio check --------------------------------------------------]]></Comment><BitSize>224</BitSize><BitOffs>7776</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>tFlowRatioFilter</Name><Type>TIME</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>8000</BitOffs><Default><DateTime>T#1M</DateTime></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rtColdStart</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Standard">R_TRIG</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ --- edge detection ----------------------------------------------------]]></Comment><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>8032</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bAnyFaultPrev</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>8096</BitOffs></SubItem><Method><Name>ResetAll</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Operator reset. Clears every latch and every filter timer unconditionally,
 then lets the next cycle re-evaluate from scratch. Anything still genuinely
 wrong re-latches immediately and the state machine refuses to leave Fault.

 This clears ALL faults, deliberately. The legacy reset cleared only fifteen
 of its bits and left the rest - notably both transducer hardware faults -
 latched until a power cycle. That is not preserved: a fault the operator
 cannot clear and cannot see the reason for is worse than one that re-trips
 honestly on the next scan.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>DINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>InhibitSensorHwEval</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Suppress the transducer health checks. The state machine asserts this on
 entry to Fault and drops it once a reset succeeds.

 Without it, a genuinely dead transducer re-latches its fault within 250 ms
 of every reset attempt and the operator can never clear the alarm to get to
 maintenance mode. The legacy solved this the same way, by gating those two
 timers on not-being-in-the-fault-stage.]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>bInhibit</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>_Report</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Capture first-out. Only the first fault in a healthy-to-faulted transition
 is recorded; later faults latch their own bits but do not overwrite the
 reported cause. This is the fix for the legacy behaviour, where the message
 register was overwritten by whichever fault happened to evaluate last in
 the scan, so the operator was routinely shown a downstream consequence
 instead of the actual trigger.]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>eErrorID</Name><Type>E_FaultId</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>DINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>sErrorString</Name><Type>STRING(30)</Type><BitSize>248</BitSize></Local></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>DWORD (1..86400)</Name><BitSize>32</BitSize><BaseType>DWORD</BaseType><Properties><Property><Name>LowerBorder</Name><Value>1</Value></Property><Property><Name>UpperBorder</Name><Value>86400</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Tc2_Utilities">E_TimeZoneID</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Time zone identifier ]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BaseType>INT</BaseType><EnumInfo><Text>eTimeZoneID_Invalid</Text><Enum>-1</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Invalid time zone ]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>eTimeZoneID_Unknown</Text><Enum>0</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Unknown time zone ]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>eTimeZoneID_Standard</Text><Enum>1</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Standard time (Winterzeit) ]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>eTimeZoneID_Daylight</Text><Enum>2</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Daylight saving time (Sommerzeit) ]]></Comment></EnumInfo></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Tc2_System">T_AmsPort</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ TwinCAT AMS port address. ]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BaseType>UINT</BaseType></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Tc2_System">ADSREAD</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ ADS read command. ]]></Comment><BitSize>1248</BitSize><SubItem><Name>NETID</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_System">T_AmsNetID</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Ams net id ]]></Comment><BitSize>192</BitSize><BitOffs>32</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>PORT</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_System">T_AmsPort</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Ads communication port ]]></Comment><BitSize>16