<BitOffs>23232</BitOffs></SubItem><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>ST_HmiSetpoints</Name><Comment><![CDATA[=============================================================================
 ST_HmiSetpoints
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Direction: Pi -> PLC (request) and PLC -> Pi (applied echo in ST_HmiStatus).
 Pi writes the whole struct, then pulses stCommand.bApplySetpoints.
 FB_Hmi clamps each value to ST_SetpointLimits before applying, and the
 clamped result is echoed in ST_HmiStatus.rSet*Applied so the UI always
 shows the truth, not the request.
=============================================================================]]></Comment><BitSize>184</BitSize><SubItem><Name>bSetPurgeOnStartup</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs><Default><Bool>false</Bool></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rSetFlow</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ requested flow setpoint      [SLM]]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>8</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rSetElevation</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ meters above seal level [MASL] ]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>40</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bSetSize25L</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ set size to 25L (default)]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>72</BitOffs><Default><Bool>true</Bool></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bSetSize50L</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ set size to 50L]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>80</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>nIp</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ EIP ip addr, subnet mask, default gateway]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>88</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>nMask</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ EIP ip addr, subnet mask, default gateway]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>120</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>nGateway</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ EIP ip addr, subnet mask, default gateway]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>152</BitOffs></SubItem><Properties><Property><Name>pack_mode</Name><Value>1</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>FB_PressureControl</Name><Comment><![CDATA[=============================================================================
 FB_PressureControl | DRAFT 8.2.26 - NOT YET VERIFIED ON HARDWARE
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 All closed-loop heater control. 

 Each loop has two parts:
   PID  -> a demand in percent
   PWM  -> that percent turned into on/off time inside a fixed period

 LOOP MAP:
   [1] Boiler / upstream pressure  PT1 -> H1   PID1
   [2] SPA (purifier) temperature  TC1 -> H2   PID2
   [3] Flow meter temperature      TC2 -> H3   PID3
   [4] External line heater        TC3 -> H4   bang-bang + hysteresis, NOT PID.

 BOILER PRESSURE SETPOINT (loop 1) has three sources, in priority order:
   1. PurgeVessel state -> purge target pressure
   2. SPA not yet flushed -> PT3 + initial dP (100 Torr)
   3. normal -> PT2 + target dP + tuning offset
 In cases 1 and 2 the PWM period is doubled while the max on-time stays
 fixed, which is how the legacy capped the boiler heater at 50 % duty.
 Once flushed, the setpoint is RAMPED at 1 Torr per 0.5 s instead of stepped.
 Drives NO coil directly. Outputs heater demands; FB_OutputHandler is the
 single writer and still gates everything on state.

 DEVIATIONS FROM THE LEGACY (all deliberate, all flagged inline):
   * gains are re-expressed in engineering units (%/Torr, %/degC) - see
     GVL_SysParameters for the conversion arithmetic. RETUNE ON THE BENCH.
   * setpoint ramp clamps at the target instead of dithering +/-1 Torr.
   * ramp is preloaded from live PT1 on enable (legacy did this only on the
     hot-restart path, rung 85).
   * derivative acts on the measurement, not the error, to kill setpoint kick.
   * SPA heater gets a hard over-temperature cut. The legacy had none.
   * external heater gets turn-off hysteresis. The legacy had none.
=============================================================================]]></Comment><BitSize>3104</BitSize><SubItem><Name>bEnable</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ FB_StateMachine.bControlEnable]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>32</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>eState</Name><Type>E_SystemState</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ needed to detect PurgeVessel & SpaFlush]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>48</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bDpControlOff</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ HMI/maint: suspend loop 1]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bTempControlOff</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ HMI/maint: suspend loop 2]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>72</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bExtHeaterEnable</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ HMI: external heater allowed]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>80</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>stProcess</Name><Type>ST_ProcessValues</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ scaled PVs]]></Comment><BitSize>496</BitSize><BitOffs>88</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>stSetpoints</Name><Type>ST_HmiSetpoints</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ operator setpoints, already clamped by FB_Hmi]]></Comment><BitSize>184</BitSize><BitOffs>584</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rTargetDiffPressure</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ [Torr] from FB_FlowCalcs]]></C