 ST_HmiCommand
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Direction: Pi -> PLC. Consume-on-read pattern:
   * Pi writes TRUE to a command bit (pyads write_by_name).
   * FB_Hmi latches it into its outputs for exactly one PLC cycle,
     then writes FALSE back. The Pi never needs to clear anything.

=============================================================================]]></Comment><BitSize>256</BitSize><SubItem><Name>nHmiHeartbeat</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Pi increments each poll cycle; never reset]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bSesOn</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ start command]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>32</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bSesOff</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ stop command ]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>40</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bSteamDeliveryOn</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ steam delivery enable]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>48</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bSteamDeliveryOff</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ steam delivery disable]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>56</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bFaultReset</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ reset all faults]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bFaultAck</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ acknowledge (silences banner, faults stay listed)]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>72</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bEnterMaint</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ request Maintenance state]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>80</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bExitMaint</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ leave Maintenance ]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>88</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>aValveCmd</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><ArrayInfo><LBound>1</LBound><Elements>4</Elements></ArrayInfo><Comment><![CDATA[ SV1 drain, SV2 main, SV3 process, SV4 water]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>96</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bDrainMode</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ drain mode]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>128</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bDpControlOn</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ suspend diff pressu